<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hsinbyushin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1736–1776</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hsinbyushin was the third king of the Konbaung dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, ruling from 1763 to 1776, a son of the dynasty's founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaungpaya">Alaungpaya</a>. His armies besieged and sacked the Siamese capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in 1767, ending the Ayutthaya Kingdom. Between 1765 and 1769 his commanders repelled four invasions by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing China</a>, and he also extended Burmese power over Manipur and the Shan and Lao states.</p></div>
